{"id":"north-coast-500","title":"North Coast 500","who":"Classic route · Scotland's Highland loop by motorcycle","when":"Best May or September–October","vehicle":"Motorcycle (or car, camper, bike), 5–7 days","kind":"moto","color":"#be185d","summary":"A loop of about 830 km from Inverness round the far north of Scotland: the Bealach na Bà pass, empty single-track roads along sea lochs, white beaches, mountains like Suilven and Stac Pollaidh, and the cliffs of the north coast. Use the passing places and expect four seasons a day.","sources":[{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: a beginner's take on the NC500","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/ride-tales/beginners-take-on-the-nc500-93251"},{"label":"Wheelworld: five on tour, mostly on two wheels","url":"https://www.wheelworldreviews.co.uk/?p=18615"}],"approximate":"The usual anticlockwise loop and overnight towns.","km":811,"bbox":[-5.813,57.3969,-3.069,58.6483],"stops":[{"name":"Inverness","place":"Inverness, Scotland","at":[57.479,-4.2257],"text":"The start and finish, at the head of the Moray Firth.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","page":"Inverness","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","credit":"Diliff","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Applecross","place":"Applecross, Scotland","at":[57.4662,-5.7348],"text":"West over the Bealach na Bà, one of the UK's steepest road climbs, hairpins and 20% gradients to 626 m.","source":{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: NC500 ride tale","url":"https://www.horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/ride-tales/beginners-take-on-the-nc500-93251"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bealach_na_Ba_Pano.jpg/500px-Bealach_na_Ba_Pano.jpg","page":"Bealach na Bà","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bealach_na_Ba_Pano.jpg","credit":"Stefan Krause, Germany","license":"FAL"}},{"name":"Torridon","place":"Torridon, Scotland","at":[57.5446,-5.5104],"text":"Along the coast road under the huge sandstone hills of Torridon.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Scotland_Torridon_village.jpg/500px-Scotland_Torridon_village.jpg","page":"Torridon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scotland_Torridon_village.jpg","credit":"Wojsyl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Gairloch","place":"Gairloch, Scotland","at":[57.728,-5.6903],"text":"Past Loch Maree to sandy bays on the Atlantic.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Loch_Maree_and_Slioch_-_geograph.org.uk_-_897208.jpg/500px-Loch_Maree_and_Slioch_-_geograph.org.uk_-_897208.jpg","page":"Loch Maree","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loch_Maree_and_Slioch_-_geograph.org.uk_-_897208.jpg","credit":"djmacpherson","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Ullapool","place":"Ullapool, Scotland","at":[57.8958,-5.1602],"text":"A white-painted fishing town on Loch Broom, ferries out to the Hebrides.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ullapool_sun.jpg/500px-Ullapool_sun.jpg","page":"Ullapool","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ullapool_sun.jpg","credit":"Paul Hart from Glasgow, Scotland","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Lochinver","place":"Lochinver, Scotland","at":[58.1524,-5.2406],"text":"The narrow coast road through Assynt: Stac Pollaidh, Suilven and bays at every bend.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/2011_Schotland_Suilven_31-05-2011_14-58-40.png/500px-2011_Schotland_Suilven_31-05-2011_14-58-40.png","page":"Suilven","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2011_Schotland_Suilven_31-05-2011_14-58-40.png","credit":"Paul Hermans","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Durness","place":"Durness, Scotland","at":[58.5467,-4.7859],"text":"The north-west corner: Smoo Cave and white beaches like Balnakeil.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Entrance_to_Smoo_Cave.jpg/500px-Entrance_to_Smoo_Cave.jpg","page":"Smoo Cave","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_to_Smoo_Cave.jpg","credit":"Florian Fuchs","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Tongue","place":"Tongue, Scotland","at":[58.4763,-4.4489],"text":"Across the causeway on the Kyle of Tongue, Ben Hope and Ben Loyal behind.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Ben_Loyal_and_the_Kyle_of_Tongue%2C_Sutherland_%283-06-2011%2C_19-25-02%29.jpg/500px-Ben_Loyal_and_the_Kyle_of_Tongue%2C_Sutherland_%283-06-2011%2C_19-25-02%29.jpg","page":"Kyle of Tongue","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ben_Loyal_and_the_Kyle_of_Tongue%2C_Sutherland_%283-06-2011%2C_19-25-02%29.jpg","credit":"2011 Schotland Ben Loyal aan Kyle of Tongue 3-06-2011 19-25-02.png: Paul Hermans *derivative work: Hogweard","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"John o' Groats","place":"John o' Groats","at":[58.6373,-3.069],"text":"Past Dunnet Head, the true northern tip of Britain, to the sea stacks of Duncansby.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG/500px-Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG","page":"Duncansby Head","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duncansby_Head_lighthouse.JPG","credit":"Russ McLean at English Wikipedia","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Wick","place":"Wick, Scotland","at":[58.4426,-3.0916],"text":"South down the east coast on faster roads.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/WickCaithness.jpg/500px-WickCaithness.jpg","page":"Wick, Caithness","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WickCaithness.jpg","credit":"Flaxton","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Dornoch","place":"Dornoch, Scotland","at":[57.8797,-4.0279],"text":"Past fairy-tale Dunrobin Castle to a cathedral town by the sea.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Dunrobin_Castle_-Sutherland_-Scotland-26May2008_%282%29.jpg/500px-Dunrobin_Castle_-Sutherland_-Scotland-26May2008_%282%29.jpg","page":"Dunrobin Castle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dunrobin_Castle_-Sutherland_-Scotland-26May2008_%282%29.jpg","credit":"Dunrobin_Castle_-Sutherland_-Scotland-26May2008.jpg: jack_spellingbacon derivative work: Snowmanradio (talk)","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Back in Inverness","place":"Inverness, Scotland","at":[57.479,-4.2257],"text":"Back over the Black Isle: about 830 km round.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg/500px-Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","page":"Inverness Castle","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","credit":"Diliff","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":134,"line":[[57.4793,-4.2261],[57.4949,-4.22],[57.5528,-4.4111],[57.579,-4.4369],[57.5584,-4.5041],[57.5629,-4.5733],[57.5914,-4.6097],[57.5939,-4.6611],[57.6229,-4.6994],[57.633,-4.7622],[57.5788,-5.0781],[57.5398,-5.1299],[57.4829,-5.3259],[57.3969,-5.5056],[57.399,-5.606],[57.4194,-5.6088],[57.4007,-5.6502],[57.4347,-5.7514],[57.4319,-5.8097],[57.4773,-5.7555]]},{"by":"ride","km":51,"line":[[57.4773,-5.7555],[57.4334,-5.813],[57.4347,-5.7514],[57.4007,-5.6502],[57.4084,-5.6205],[57.4415,-5.5813],[57.4604,-5.5831],[57.524,-5.6458],[57.5271,-5.5274],[57.5446,-5.5104]]},{"by":"ride","km":48,"line":[[57.5446,-5.5104],[57.567,-5.3469],[57.5823,-5.3132],[57.6045,-5.3034],[57.6757,-5.4676],[57.6924,-5.558],[57.6878,-5.6581],[57.728,-5.6903]]},{"by":"ride","km":89,"line":[[57.728,-5.6903],[57.75,-5.5963],[57.7651,-5.6041],[57.7976,-5.5712],[57.804,-5.5848],[57.8372,-5.5788],[57.865,-5.5416],[57.8509,-5.4546],[57.8643,-5.4367],[57.8786,-5.4411],[57.8845,-5.4081],[57.8307,-5.1866],[57.8065,-5.151],[57.7849,-5.1647],[57.737,-5.0892],[57.7585,-5.0392],[57.75